## Interface: 16001
## Title: Rude Boy
## Notes: Hides chat lines that contain your filtered words, or that come from players and guilds you filter, and warns you when one of them is in your group.
## Author: Zack
## Version: 0.1.0
## SavedVariables: RudeBoyDB
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\Spell_Holy_Silence
## Category: Chat
## X-License: MIT
## X-Website: https://github.com/wongz1/rudeboy_addon

# NOTE: 16001 is copied from CatFacts, which derived it from the WoW Forever beta client 1.60.1.
# To confirm, run in game:  /run print((select(4, GetBuildInfo())))
# If the addon shows as "out of date", tick "Load out of date AddOns" on the AddOns screen.

# Saved.lua works around a WoW Forever beta bug: the client writes addon settings to
# WTF/Account/<account>/SavedVariables/RudeBoy.lua but never reads them back. When Saved.lua is a
# link to that file (tools/link-saved-settings.sh), the last save is loaded here as code. It is
# fine for the file to be missing: the game skips it. Once Blizzard fixes the loader, the real
# settings load afterwards and take over.
Saved.lua
Core.lua
Chat.lua
Group.lua
Scan.lua
UI.lua
Commands.lua
